{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T11:55:56.553Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of the work:\n\n**Task 1** — When a land moves the default branch and `vcs.afterLand` is set, osq runs it in the checkout, records a failure, and retries on the next land of that change.\n\nChanged files (all inside scope):\n- `src/core/foundation/config-vcs.ts` — added optional `afterLand`, trimmed/validated through `trimmedField`.\n- `src/core/vcs/land-after.ts` (new) — runs the command in the `prepare` role via `runVerificationCommand`, writes/clears `after-land.json` in `watchStateDir(projectRoot, home)`, exports `readAfterLandFailure` for task 2, and `runAfterLand`/`retryAfterLand`.\n- `src/core/vcs/land.ts` — `LandResult.afterLand`, `LandOptions.home`, runs after worktree cleanup, retries an already-landed change only when the record names it, failure exits 1. Stays at 249 lines with `landChange` inside the 80-line function budget.\n- `src/cli/land.ts` — `home` option forwarded to `landChange`, `REBUILD_MESSAGE` suppressed when the command ran and passed.\n- `tests/vcs-land-after.test.ts` (new) — 10 tests covering all six version-control after-land scenarios, the cli-foundation \"into osq itself\" scenario, and the two config scenarios.\n\nVerification:\n- Task verify: 10/10 pass.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: exit 0 (typecheck, UI typecheck, build, full suite, lint).\n- Result written to `openspec/changes/166-land-runs-after-command/.run/results/1.md`.\n\nOne documented deviation: `landCommand` forwards `home` to `landChange`, but the `publish` path can't thread it because `src/core/vcs/land-publish.ts` is outside scope; the command still runs after the push."}}
